# Note: the tf_calib file is only used to identify calibrators and their
# respective values of m and M.  However, the value of M in the calib file
# depends on the estimated calibrator ("host") distance, which will be 
# replaced by the host distance determined from the distance network.
# Therefore duplicate values are not needed, and are in fact problematic.
# In this file duplicate calibrators are removed, and the columns mu_host,
# mu_error, anchor, source, and method are not used in the processing.
# (Some versions of the code might read them for verification purposes.)
#
# Also note that the internal logic of the main code will prevent NGC 4258
# to be used as a host; there is nothing fundamental about it, but the
# mechanism is different since mu_n4258 is not currently a parameter, and the
# relevant equation would need to have a different form.
#
